\ A cleanup quotation's own failure is suppressed, and suppression must be complete: the
\ body's propagating error keeps its type, message, and frames, with nothing from the
\ cleanup failure bleeding in. No flags, so the interpreted and eager suites bind one
\ golden and the compiled cleanup path is covered by the rerun.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "body failed" body-error: make-error throw ] ;
spoil: ( -- ) [ f "cleanup failed" cleanup-error: make-error throw ] ;

[ boom ] [ spoil ] cleanup
